WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.100
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:06.745 --> 00:00:09.129
Give me one minute,
and I'll show you how Cloud SQL

00:00:09.129 --> 00:00:11.798
can help you save time
in developing your next great app.

00:00:12.142 --> 00:00:14.756
Cloud SQL is a fully-managed
relational database service

00:00:14.757 --> 00:00:17.808
from MySQL, Postgre,
or SQL Server on Google Cloud.

00:00:18.155 --> 00:00:20.549
It lets you hand off
mundane, time-consuming tasks,

00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:22.721
like patches, updates,
backups, and replicas,

00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:24.748
so you can focus on building your app!

00:00:24.852 --> 00:00:27.089
Cloud SQL integrates
with BigQuery for analytics

00:00:27.089 --> 00:00:29.910
or connects as a backend
to your App Engine, Compute Engine,

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:30.938
or Kubernetes apps.

00:00:31.262 --> 00:00:33.308
Setting up Cloud SQL
is quick and seamless.

00:00:33.308 --> 00:00:36.216
In a snap, you can create
in an instant with the Cloud console

00:00:36.216 --> 00:00:38.689
by choosing the type
of database version and location

00:00:38.689 --> 00:00:40.177
or use the <i>gcloud</i> command line.

00:00:40.365 --> 00:00:43.556
Then you're ready to upload your data
and connect your applications.

00:00:43.557 --> 00:00:47.456
To go further, set up automatic backups,
replication, and failover,

00:00:47.457 --> 00:00:50.835
so you can create a highly-available
database for critical applications.

00:00:51.295 --> 00:00:53.489
You get full encryption
at rest and in transit,

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:55.787
keeping your private data
safe and compliant.

00:00:56.638 --> 00:00:59.872
External connections can be encrypted
using SSL or Cloud SQL proxy.

00:01:00.182 --> 00:01:03.023
Being a relational database,
Cloud SQL is great for OLTP

00:01:03.024 --> 00:01:05.882
where frequent queries
and fast response time are needed.

00:01:05.882 --> 00:01:08.889
You can use it to manage everything
from a single WordPress blog

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.443
to a global aggregation
of wheat crops and rainfall.

00:01:11.443 --> 00:01:14.569
Next time you're looking
for a quick relational database solution,

00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:16.255
take a minute to try out Cloud SQL.

00:01:16.422 --> 00:01:19.555
To learn more, check out
<i>cloud.google.com/sql.</i>

